# Design Principles (Apply These)

- **Motion has meaning.** Nothing animates without a reason. Easing curves matter.
  Ease-out for entrances, ease-in for exits, spring physics for interactive elements.
- **Spatial consistency.** The room metaphor requires consistent sense of depth and
  directionality. Camera/viewport transitions should feel like movement, not cuts.
- **Performance is part of the design.** Target 60fps on everything interactive.
  Use `will-change`, `transform`, and `opacity` for GPU-composited animations only.
- **Details are the product.** Hover states, focus rings, loading states — these are
  not afterthoughts.

